<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ming treasure voyages</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1405">1405</a>–<a href="/years/1433">1433</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as expeditions led by Zheng He, maritime expeditions led by Zheng He</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ming treasure voyages were seven large maritime expeditions led by the admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-he">Zheng He</a> between 1405 and 1433. Huge fleets sailed through South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>, displaying Ming power and collecting tribute. The voyages were ended and not resumed, reflecting a shift in Ming priorities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ming-treasure-voyages.jpg" alt="Ming treasure voyages" width="320" height="361" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ZhengHeShips.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
